                <pb facs="0854" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg742"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Moffat to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Moffat reports that Gen. Estrada and the leaders of the revolution, having
                    terminated a conference lasting several hours, have signified to him in a signed
                    document their desire to terminate hostilities through the mediation of the
                    United States, agreeing to terms of peace on the following bases: The United
                    States to designate <pb facs="0855" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/> a provisional
                    President, who shall be other than Madriz or Estrada, the person named to
                    immediately order an election of a constitutional President; the United States
                    to supervise the free election of the same; neither Madriz nor Estrada to be a
                    candidate. Adds that the Government of Nicaragua is to recognize the public
                    debts incurred by the revolution, and that the abolition of unconstitutional
                    monopolies is provided for.</p>
            </div>
